+# Soft-float (PS2Float) port — implementation log
+
+Branch `stuntman-softfloat`, off `movietheater-lrps2` @ `2cf344b`.
+
+Goal: make Stuntman (SLUS-20250) level-4 recorded-input chase playback deterministic, by
+emulating the PS2 FPU/VU floating point bit-exactly instead of using the host SSE units.
+This is a backport of **PCSX2 PR #12001** (`GitHubProUser67:soft-float-int` — adds
+`pcsx2/PS2Float.cpp/.h` and rewrites the COP1 + VU *interpreters* to use it) combined with
+**Goatman13's `int_fallback_fpu_cop2` routing** (described in PCSX2 issue #2990 — the
+recompilers hand the affected opcodes to those interpreter bodies).
+
+Everything is behind a new core option and is **off by default**. With the option off the
+core is behaviourally identical to `2cf344b` for every game.
+
+---
+
+## Core options (libretro)
+
+| token | values | default |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `pcsx2_softfloat` | `disabled` / `enabled` | `disabled` |
+| `pcsx2_softfloat_scope` | `All` / `Add/Sub + Mul` / `Add/Sub only` / `Div/Sqrt only` | `All` |
+| `pcsx2_softfloat_vu0micro` | `interpreter` / `recompiler` | `interpreter` |
+
+### What each knob actually gates (read this before designing an arm)
+
+`pcsx2_softfloat_scope` **narrows COP1 only.**
+
+* COP1 (`iFPU.cpp`) tests the mask **per op**, so a narrow scope genuinely leaves ops on the
+  recompiler: `Add/Sub + Mul` keeps `DIV_S/SQRT_S/RSQRT_S` recompiled; `Add/Sub only` also
+  keeps `MUL_S/MULA_S` and the whole MADD/MSUB family (they need both bits).
+* COP2 (`microVU_Macro.inl`) tests `CHECK_VU_SOFT(0)` for **non-zero**, so *any* scope routes
+  all 75 ops to the interpreter. The per-family guards inside `VUops.cpp` then pick PS2Float
+  vs the original hard-float body — i.e. scope changes the math, not the routing.
+* `pcsx2_softfloat_vu0micro` is independent of scope and of the mask.
+
+`pcsx2_softfloat_vu0micro` decides only whether VU0 **micro** programs (CALLMS) run on
+`CpuIntVU0`. COP2 **macro** mode is diverted to the soft-float interpreter either way.
+
+Both are read **once**, in `check_variables(first_run == true)` in `libretro/main.cpp`, before
+`VMManager::ApplySettings()` and the VM boot. They are *Restart* options by nature: the
+recompilers bake the routing decision into the blocks they emit, so flipping them mid-run
+would leave stale blocks. They are not re-read in the `check_variables(false)` path.
+
+`pcsx2_softfloat` and `pcsx2_softfloat_scope` map onto three new
+`Pcsx2Config::RecompilerOptions` fields, written as `EmuCore/CPU/Recompiler` ints:
+
+* `fpuSoftFloat` — EE COP1
+* `vu0SoftFloat` — COP2 macro mode + VU0 micro programs
+* `vu1SoftFloat` — **always written as 0**. VU1 is graphics-only; soft-floating it would
+  cost a great deal for no gain on this bug.
+
+The value is a mask of `SOFT_FLOAT_ADDSUB (0x1)` / `SOFT_FLOAT_MUL (0x2)` /
+`SOFT_FLOAT_DIVSQRT (0x4)`, exactly as upstream. The `_scope` option exists only because the
+PR already carried that granularity; `All` (7) is the accurate setting.
+
+## What is routed where, when enabled
+
+* **EE FPU (COP1)** — the recompiler emits a call to the COP1 interpreter op for
+  `ADD_S ADDA_S SUB_S SUBA_S MUL_S MULA_S MADD_S MADDA_S MSUB_S MSUBA_S DIV_S SQRT_S RSQRT_S`
+  (13 ops). `ABS_S NEG_S MOV_S MAX_S MIN_S C_EQ C_LE C_LT CVT_S CVT_W` stay recompiled — the
+  PR does not change their arithmetic, so there is nothing to gain and a real cost to pay.
+* **COP2 / VU0 macro mode** — the recompiler emits a call to the COP2 interpreter entry point
+  for **all 75 ops whose `REC_COP2_mVU0` mode has bit `0x10`** (writes status/mac): the whole
+  ADD/ADDA/SUB/SUBA/MUL/MULA/MADD/MADDA/MSUB/MSUBA families incl. every `.i/.q/.x/.y/.z/.w`
+  broadcast, plus `OPMULA OPMSUB DIV SQRT RSQRT`. `MAX/MINI/CLIP/ABS/ITOF/FTOI/MOVE/MR32` and
+  the integer ops stay in macro mode.
+* **VU0 micro programs (CALLMS/CALLMSR)** — `CpuVU0` is switched to `CpuIntVU0` **only if
+  `pcsx2_softfloat_vu0micro = interpreter`** (the default). This is driven through the stock
+  `EnableVU0` setting from `libretro/main.cpp`, so all the existing plumbing applies:
+  `microVU0` stays reserved and is explicitly `Reset()` by `ClearCPUExecutionCaches`, because
+  COP2 macro mode still emits through it for the ops that are *not* diverted.
+* **VU1** — untouched, fully recompiled.
+
